# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds TENANT_ID / CLIENT_ID / CLIENT_SECRET for the Azure app registration
# that has write access to the live SharePoint site. It must never be committed,
# to a private repo either: git history is permanent and a repo's visibility can
# be changed later. .env.example carries the same keys with the values stripped.
.env
local.settings.json

# ── Candidate data (PII) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real applicants: names, email addresses, phone numbers, locations, resumes.
candidates.db
candidates.db-shm
candidates.db-wal
candidates.db.bak*
*.xlsx
P2_Logs/
P2_Input/
P2_Output/
P2_Final_Results/
P2_Preview/
resume_cache/
processing_artifacts/
benchmark_resumes/
tmp/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.png

# ── Environment and build noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
*.lock
# jd_roles_cache.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the cached job-description
# set the scorer matches against, it carries no personal data, and shipping it means a
# fresh clone can score without first fetching every JD.
